            "text": "{\"findings\":[{\"tipo\":\"GPU\",\"causa_raiz\":\"O tempo de renderizacao na GPU atingiu 30.19ms contra o teto de 16.7ms (violacoes acumuladas: 514 frames), indicando sobrecarga massiva no fill rate, shaders excessivamente complexos ou custo elevado de efeitos de pos-processamento em resolucao nativa para a GTX 1650.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using UnityEngine;\\\\nusing UnityEngine.Rendering;\\\\n\\\\npublic class PerformanceScaler : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float targetFrameRate = 60.0f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float minResolutionScale = 0.70f;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private float maxResolutionScale = 1.0f;\\\\n    private float currentScale = 1.0f;\\\\n\\\\n    void Awake()\\\\n    {\\\\n        Application.targetFrameRate = 60;\\\\n        QualitySettings.vSyncCount = 0;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    void Update()\\\\n    {\\\\n        float currentFps = 1.0f / Mathf.Max(Time.unscaledDeltaTime, 0.0001f);\\\\n        if (currentFps \u003c targetFrameRate - 5f && currentScale \u003e minResolutionScale)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Max(minResolutionScale, currentScale - 0.05f * Time.unscaledDeltaTime);\\\\n            ScalableBufferManager.ResizeBuffers(currentScale, currentScale);\\\\n        }\\\\n        else if (currentFps \u003e= targetFrameRate && currentScale \u003c maxResolutionScale)\\\\n        {\\\\n            currentScale = Mathf.Min(maxResolutionScale, currentScale + 0.02f * Time.unscaledDeltaTime);\\\\n            ScalableBufferManager.ResizeBuffers(currentScale, currentScale);\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"A placa de video esta demorando quase o dobro do tempo permitido para pintar os pixels da tela. Para resolver isso, usamos uma resolucao dinamica que reduz suavemente a quantidade de pixels desenhados quando o jogo fica pesado, aliviando a placa de video sem que o jogador perceba quedas bruscas de frames.\"},{\"tipo\":\"GC\",\"causa_raiz\":\"Picos de Garbage Collector pausando o loop principal (5.61ms de coleta com alocacoes de ate 98KB por frame), gerando microtravamentos causados por instanciacao dinamica repetitiva ou criacao de objetos descartaveis na memoria.\",\"codigo_refatorado\":\"using System.Collections.Generic;\\\\nusing UnityEngine;\\\\n\\\\npublic class SimpleObjectPool : MonoBehaviour\\\\n{\\\\n    public static SimpleObjectPool Instance { get; private set; }\\\\n    [SerializeField] private GameObject prefab;\\\\n    [SerializeField] private int initialSize = 50;\\\\n    private readonly Queue\u003cGameObject\u003e pool = new Queue\u003cGameObject\u003e();\\\\n\\\\n    void Awake()\\\\n    {\\\\n        Instance = this;\\\\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c initialSize; i++)\\\\n        {\\\\n            GameObject obj = Instantiate(prefab, transform);\\\\n            obj.SetActive(false);\\\\n            pool.Enqueue(obj);\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public GameObject Get()\\\\n    {\\\\n        GameObject obj = pool.Count \u003e 0 ? pool.Dequeue() : Instantiate(prefab, transform);\\\\n        obj.SetActive(true);\\\\n        return obj;\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    public void ReturnToPool(GameObject obj)\\\\n    {\\\\n        obj.SetActive(false);\\\\n        pool.Enqueue(obj);\\\\n    }\\\\n}\",\"explicacao_didatica\":\"Quando voce cria e destroi objetos constantemente com Instantiate e Destroy, a memoria fica cheia de lixo e a Unity pausa o jogo para limpar (Garbage Collection). O Pooling reutiliza objetos desativando-os em vez de destrui-los, eliminando essas travadinhas.\"}],\"dicas_level_design\":null}",
